\begin{proof}
The theorem is false as stated. Take $k=1$, $\mathbf{x}=(0)\in R^1$, and $\mathbf{y}=(1)\in R^1$. Then $\mathbf{y}\neq 0$, but $\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{y}=0\cdot1=0$. Hence such a $\mathbf{y}$ does exist.
