\begin{proof}
The statement cannot be proved because it is false. Let $k=1$, $\mathbf{x}=(0)$, and $\mathbf{y}=(1)$. Then $\mathbf{y}\neq 0$ while $\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{y}=0$. This is a counterexample.
\end{proof}
